it_fancy_vocab_129	the Monoculture	de:K The figurative Monokultur of technology and institutions is productive critical vocabulary that encodes shared dependencies and correlated risks. || es:K The technology and institutional metaphor is productive critical vocabulary that encodes shared dependency and correlated systemic risk. || fr:K The technology and institutional metaphor encodes uniform dependency and correlated systemic risk, teaching substantially more than the literal agricultural cognate. || it:K The technology-dependency metaphor teaches monocoltura tecnologica, including correlated systemic risk and the contrast with the distinct cultural noun monocultura. || pt:K A metáfora monocultura tecnológica codifica dependências comuns e riscos sistêmicos correlacionados, acrescentando valor além do cognato agrícola.
it_fancy_vocab_130	the Asymmetry	de:D Die Asymmetrie is a transparent, familiar academic cognate; the bare source adds no specific relational frame or semantic contrast. || es:D La asimetría is a transparent, familiar academic cognate; the isolated source gives no specific information, power or relational frame to distinguish it. || fr:D L’asymétrie is a transparent, familiar academic cognate; the isolated source gives no information, power or relational frame that would make it distinctively teachable. || it:D L'asimmetria is a transparent, familiar academic cognate; the isolated source gives no information, power or relational frame that would make it distinctively teachable. || pt:D A assimetria é um cognato acadêmico transparente e familiar; o original não seleciona assimetria de informação, poder ou outra moldura específica.
it_fancy_vocab_131	the Contingency	de:K The theoretical Kontingenz must be distinguished from the emergency, eventuality and backup-plan senses commonly carried by English contingency. || es:K The item supports the theoretical sense of contingencia and distinguishes non-necessity from the common emergency or backup-plan senses. || fr:K The theoretical sense of contingence as non-necessity must be distinguished from an unforeseen event and from the English contingency-plan sense. || it:K The theoretical sense of contingenza as non-necessity must be distinguished from an unforeseen event and from the English contingency-plan sense. || pt:K A acepção teórica de contingência como não necessidade precisa ser distinguida do imprevisto e do plano de contingência operacional.
